🎯 Two Pointers Mastery Roadmap
Think of Two Pointers as a family of techniques, not one algorithm.
                         TWO POINTERS
                              │
        ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
        ↓                     ↓                     ↓
   Opposite Ends         Same Direction       Multiple/Advanced
        │                     │                     │
        ↓                     ↓                     ↓
   left + right           slow + fast        3Sum / 4Sum
   sorted arrays          sliding boundary    Partitioning
   palindrome             in-place           Merge techniques
   pair problems          duplicate removal   Advanced variants

🏆 The order I recommend YOU practice

Don't randomly solve 50 Two-Pointer questions.

Follow this progression:

Phase 1 — Foundation
Reverse Array
Reverse String
Valid Palindrome
Two Sum II
Pair Sum in Sorted Array
Phase 2 — Slow/Fast
Remove Element
Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array
Move Zeroes
Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array II
Phase 3 — Two Sorted Arrays
Merge Sorted Array
Intersection of Two Arrays
Intersection of Two Arrays II
Is Subsequence
Phase 4 — Three Pointers / Partitioning
Sort Colors
Partition Array
Dutch National Flag
Phase 5 — 3Sum Family
3Sum
3Sum Closest
4Sum
Phase 6 — Optimization
Container With Most Water
Trapping Rain Water
Phase 7 — Advanced Variants
Valid Palindrome II
Backspace String Compare
Boats to Save People
Squares of a Sorted Array
Interval-related pointer techniques
Advanced two-pointer + greedy problems
